description = [=[[b]This mod is whitelisted.[/b]

mod id 3790290682

[b]Small additions that help commanders, players and spectators read the game.[/b] Most of what this mod started with is now part of NS2 itself: build 345 brought it into the base game (see "Gone vanilla" below). Here is what the mod still adds.

[h1]What it adds[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Welder icon on nameplates.[/b] A marine teammate carrying a welder gets a welder icon beside their name, so nobody has to ask who has one. Seen by the marine commander, and by marines whenever that teammate's nameplate shows.
[*] [b]Commander hotkey labels.[/b] Optional, off by default: each commander button shows its hotkey in its corner, following your own key bindings. Useful for new commanders.
[*] [b]Nutrient mist indicators.[/b] The alien commander sees a green badge over every lifeform egg and structure the mist is helping: eggs evolving faster, structures still growing, and disconnected cysts it keeps alive. Fully grown structures get no badge, since the mist does nothing for them. A player evolving in a misted egg gets a mist icon in the HUD's status row.
[*] [b]Shield bar for aliens.[/b] With Centralized HUD bars, your mucous, vampirism and babbler shields show as one bar beside your health bar, with their total underneath. A full bar is all three shields at their maximum for your lifeform at biomass 1, so the same fill always means the same protection.
[*] [b]Tech maps for spectators.[/b] Hold your tech map key and press 1 or 2 for the marine or alien map: the same controls as NSL Mod's, by Dragon.
[*] [b]Ready state on the scoreboard.[/b] Under Shine's tournament mode each team's header shows ready (green tick) or not ready (red cross) until the round starts. A player joining mid pre-game may see a team as not ready until its state next changes.
[/list]

[h1]Gone vanilla[/h1]
Build 345 made these part of NS2 itself, so the mod no longer adds them. Most are switches under Options, Advanced.
[list]
[*] Research time, cooldown, health, armor and speed on commander tooltips, Bone Wall's health at your biomass level, and the ARC's deployed stats.
[*] The "In Cooldown" panel for the whole team, and the cooldown dial being right whoever is in the chair.
[*] Biomass and research in each hive's row of the alien hive panel.
[*] Several biomass levels researching at once, on the tech map and on the biomass bar.
[*] Supply icons on tooltips matching the top bar, and supply on the spectator bar.
[*] Lost arms lab upgrades staying on the marine HUD in red.
[*] Marine blips colored by weapon, with your own colors if you like.
[*] Phase gate arrows on the commander and spectator minimap.
[*] Exo weapon bars beside the crosshair.
[/list]

[h1]Settings[/h1]
Options, Mods, "Bleu's Improved Tooltips": hotkey labels, the welder icon and the shield bar.

[h1]Servers[/h1]
The mod does not change gameplay. The server's only part is sending a team's tech tree to spectators who ask for it.

It does have to be installed on the server. NS2's default consistency check restricts which mod entry files a client is allowed to load, so on a server running stock settings the server needs this mod too. If you want it on a server you play on, ask the admin to add it.

Source: https://github.com/Bleuitup/Bleus-Improved-Tooltips]=]
